The Man Who Sold the Eiffel Tower · 3D YouTube Short (1080×1920)

Picture: modelled, lit and animated in code with three.js (MIT). Post (depth of field, ambient occlusion, bloom, grade):
core/three/post.js from the Lemo-Opuscar library (github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, MIT). Characters (sculpted heads with
painted faces, tailored 1920s suits), sets (the Eiffel Tower, a Haussmann boulevard, the hotel salon, the hotel front and a
police station) and props are built from primitives for this film. Historical people appear as stylised stand-ins with no
real likeness. Hotel name and the ministry on the letter are historical; the newspaper ("Le Quotidien") is invented.

Font: Fredoka — Milena Brandão / Google Fonts, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (fonts/OFL-Fredoka.txt; files from the @fontsource npm package).

Music and sound effects: synthesized in code (music.py; synth_lib.py from the Lemo-Opuscar library, MIT). No samples.

